# A Edwards Decorating — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. On a host, set these in its environment.
#
# IMPORTANT: the site is prerendered, so these are read at BUILD time, not per
# request. Setting one on a host that is already running changes nothing until
# the site is rebuilt. Set them, then deploy.

# ── The site's own address ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for canonical URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt, the share image and the
# structured data. Falls back to https://www.aedwardsdecorating.co.uk, which is
# the domain LAUNCH.md step 1 recommends registering — it was available on
# 11 August 2026 but nobody has bought it yet.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.aedwardsdecorating.co.uk

# ── Enquiry delivery ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The contact form does not render at all unless one of the two options below
# is configured. That is deliberate: Andy has no email address on file yet, and
# a form that silently drops enquiries is worse than no form. With neither set,
# the contact field shows his phone number instead.
#
# Option 1 — POST each enquiry as JSON to whatever he ends up using
# (a form service, a Zap, an inbox bridge). Simplest thing that works.
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=https://example.com/hooks/enquiry

# Option 2 — send it as an email. Both of these are required together.
# ENQUIRY_TO=andy@aedwardsdecorating.co.uk
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Optional. Must be an address on a domain verified with the mail provider,
# otherwise the send is rejected. Defaults to enquiries@aedwardsdecorating.co.uk
# ENQUIRY_FROM=enquiries@aedwardsdecorating.co.uk
